In article <2u607g$hk2@news.doit.wisc.edu> tomas@cae.wisc.edu (Tomas Charles Willis) writes:

TW> I recently DL'd the `official NetHack Amiga (3.1) binaries' from Aminet
TW> unpacked them and started spending my time.  Alas, NetHack cannot find
TW> the fun levels (oracle.lev, orcus.lev, etc) and just gives me boring
TW> mazes.  Is this a common problem with this distruibution or just
TW> my boneheaded installation?

You must search for this line in NetHack.cnf:

# The search path for files like record, help, opthelp, etc.
PATH=NetHack:

and change it to:

PATH=NetHack:;HackExe:

